  "scout_brief": "Focus: observability & reporting \u2014 logging, metrics (/metrics, Prometheus), and operator-facing reporting (daily-report, marker/corpus-version reporting, ops dashboards). MOTIVATING BUG (just root-caused): ingest/store.py::write_chunks writes corpus-version.json with chunk_count=len(chunks)/paper_count from only the LAST per-paper batch (bulk_ingest + re_embed call it once per paper), so notebook markers read chunk_count=106 while the real table has 10298 rows \u2014 a ~100x silent discrepancy that NOTHING flagged (it surfaced only by manual inspection during the live cutover). Scout for capabilities that would make this CLASS of bug \u2014 a persisted metadata field silently diverging from ground truth, and wrong values in startup logs / reports going unnoticed \u2014 easy to catch automatically: e.g. invariant/consistency checks at write or startup (marker counts vs table row count), structured logging with assertable fields, metrics that expose ground-truth vs recorded deltas, a reporting/diff surface, drift/regression alarms. Bias toward LOCAL-FIRST, single-workstation, no-new-heavy-infra options consistent with arXMCP's constraints.",
